// A statement a theory's completed rules rewrite to two normal forms is no
// rule the theory derives: the twin of the model's `invMul`. Commutativity
// holds in the parity group, but the group's rules leave its two sides apart,
// and a group need not be abelian.

// The group's unit, associativity and inverse laws.
import "../../model/identity/group-laws.gandr" ;

/// Commutativity, refused: its sides are their own normal forms.
@[ refuses("UnderivedRule") ]
derive comm : mul(x, y) <=> mul(y, x) in Group
